# Start or skip a workout. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### A rest day → 409 workout.nothing_planned. Plan a routine on today to get a 201.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-01-05",
  "status": "skipped"
}

### Start today's workout → 201 with a routine planned on today, or 409 workout.another_in_progress.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-01-05",
  "status": "inProgress"
}

### Start an empty workout today → 201 named Workout, with no routine and no exercises, or 409 workout.another_in_progress.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-01-05",
  "status": "inProgress",
  "empty": true
}

### Empty while skipping → 400 validation, with an error for empty.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-01-05",
  "status": "skipped",
  "empty": true
}

### A day that hasn't come yet → 409 workout.date_in_the_future.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2099-01-05",
  "status": "skipped"
}

### No date → 400 validation.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "skipped"
}

### Not signed in → 401 unauthorized.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workouts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-01-05",
  "status": "skipped"
}
